Background information:

Thursday evening I lost a character when attacked by a hungry and confused
kitten in a corridor.  (I would not back away due to a boulder, had injured
my foot earlier so I couldn't kick, had tried tossing all food towards the
animal and by the time I remembered there was an option to prevent the
annoying "You stop to avoid hitting Bo.  Bo hits you." messages I had died.

Friday morning a coworker was having fun picking up all of the neat stuff
he found lying around on level 4 (where I died) when he fell into a pit
just after defeating a monster.  Up walks a [hungry] kitten.  End of
second character.

Today, I deliberately tried to clear out level 4.  I went down there with
tripe rations and re-tamed this kitten and the other pet (from my coworker)
when "Hayduke's ghost touched you!  Bear's ghost touched you!".

Yes, this level is becoming a regular cemetary.  A shopkeeper has moved
in since there is _so much_ stuff lying around.  (I am not kidding.
There has been a shopkeeper in this level for the past 4-5 games).

Last time I found (created) an aligned altar and sacrificed everything
I killed.  Between that (which gave me an artifact) and a potion of  
gain-level I lifted from a shopkeeper, I thought I was ready for anything.

After all, a level 5 (or 6 ?) character with 60+ hp should be able to
handle a ghost or two, right?  Wrong!  (I died from a hidden mimic, but was
weakened by the ghosts earlier).

So, any suggestions on what we can do from within the game?  Most of
the people here have trouble getting to the fourth level in the first
place (only "Hayduke" and myself regularly get down there), and for
them I am thinking about nuking the bones file unless someone has a
better idea.


